<p>UK insurance brokers are caught between rising regulatory demands, increasing competition from direct-to-consumer platforms, and client expectations for faster, more personalised service. AI is helping forward-thinking brokers do more with their existing teams, improving service levels whilst reducing operational costs.</p>
<p>Generic AI tools fall short in insurance because they don't understand the regulatory environment or the complexity of insurance products. A generic document processor can't extract the right fields from a loss report. A generic chatbot can't answer nuanced questions about policy coverage or excess. Generic fraud detection doesn't know what normal looks like in your book of business, so it flags everything or nothing.</p>
<p>Bespoke AI solutions are trained on your data and built for your product lines. We create risk assessment models that understand your underwriting appetite and the specific risk factors relevant to your product range. We build claims processing that extracts data from the document types you actually receive, not generic templates. We implement fraud detection calibrated to your historical claims data, so the anomalies it flags are genuinely suspicious, not noise.</p>
<p>Compliance is non-negotiable in UK insurance. The FCA requires rigorous oversight of advice, claims handling, and customer communications. AI systems in insurance must be explainable, auditable, and free from bias in pricing and underwriting decisions. We build with the FCA's consumer duty in mind, ensuring AI assists rather than replaces human judgement on regulated activities. All personal data processing is UK GDPR compliant, with clear audit trails for every AI-assisted decision.</p>
<p>We worked with a UK commercial insurance broker placing £40m GWP across SME and mid-market clients. Claims handling was creating a backlog, with average processing times exceeding 15 working days. Our AI claims triage and data extraction system, integrated with their Acturis broking platform, reduced average processing time to 6 working days and eliminated the backlog within two months. The compliance monitoring module flagged three potential conduct issues in its first quarter that had been missed by manual review, all resolved before any client impact.</p>

